# Orca native worktree

`using-git-worktrees` Step 1a prefers a native worktree tool. When both of the following are true, the Orca CLI is that tool. Create the worktree with it. Skip Step 1b. Do not run [`git worktree add`](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-worktree).

- `.claude/skills/orca-cli/SKILL.md` exists.
- This session is an Orca session: `ORCA_CLI_COMMAND` is set, `ORCA_DEV_REPO_ROOT` is set, or the terminal is Orca-managed.

Resolve the executable and the flags by following the `orca-cli` skill. Do not invent flags. Do not run `ORCA open` to make this rule apply.

If either condition is false, follow `using-git-worktrees` as written, including Step 1b.
